<%#
  The locked state of a Pro card — what an org whose plan doesn't include the
  feature sees in place of the real thing. Same shape everywhere (the
  production Pay tab set the pattern): padlock in a pink square, the feature's
  own headline, one line on why it's Pro, and an Upgrade to Pro button that
  opens the upgrade modal (and falls back to the billing upgrade page without
  JS). Render it INSIDE the card body so the card keeps its header + Pro pill.

  Locals:
    feature     (required) PAID_FEATURES symbol — money, contracts, agreements…
    title       (required) what the card would be about, e.g. "Performers are paid for this production"
    description (required) one sentence on what Pro adds
  NOTE: keep ERB tags out of this comment.
%>
<div class="flex items-start gap-4">
  <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-lg bg-pink-100 text-pink-500 flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0">
    <svg class="w-5 h-5" fill="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 20 20" aria-label="Pro feature"><path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M5 9V7a5 5 0 0110 0v2a2 2 0 012 2v5a2 2 0 01-2 2H5a2 2 0 01-2-2v-5a2 2 0 012-2zm8-2v2H7V7a3 3 0 016 0z" clip-rule="evenodd"/></svg>
  </div>
  <div class="flex-1 min-w-0">
    <p class="font-medium text-gray-900"><%= title %></p>
    <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 mt-1"><%= description %></p>
    <div class="mt-4">
      <%= render "shared/button", text: "Upgrade to Pro", variant: "primary", size: "medium",
            path: manage_billing_upgrade_path(feature: feature.to_s),
            data: { action: "click->upgrade-modal#open", upgrade_feature: feature.to_s } %>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
